import{_ as a,o as t,c as i,a5 as n}from"./chunks/framework.CsGesDJn.js";const m=JSON.parse('{"title":"Cases","description":"","frontmatter":{},"headers":[],"relativePath":"feature/media-package-campaign/request-completion-validation/test.md","filePath":"feature/media-package-campaign/request-completion-validation/test.md"}'),r={name:"feature/media-package-campaign/request-completion-validation/test.md"};function o(s,e,l,d,c,p){return t(),i("div",null,[...e[0]||(e[0]=[n('<h1 id="cases" tabindex="-1">Cases <a class="header-anchor" href="#cases" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Cases&quot;">​</a></h1><ul><li><p>UI refinement: today vs future Campaign start chooses the later; inclusive final day; expired/invalid timeline has no selectable range. Workspace timezone different from browser and DST boundaries yield correct instant bounds. Create and edit use the same bounds; do not auto-clamp old values. Picker min/max, manual entry inline/native validation, loading/failure/retry save disabled, periodic/focus bounds refresh. API validation retained. vi/en, light/dark and mobile smoke.</p></li><li><p>Manager completion cancels PENDING only; completed status prevents creation/edit/receipt, IN_PROGRESS acceptance/denial remains available.</p></li><li><p>Concurrent receive versus completion resolves by agreement lock; Mongo atomic predicates never cancel IN_PROGRESS.</p></li><li><p>Outbox failure leaves entry; retry after Mongo success before SQL acknowledgement does not duplicate history/version.</p></li><li><p>Unauthorized/invalid completion never enqueues. SQL rollback never exposes queue job.</p></li><li><p>Deadline today/start/end accepted, yesterday/before-start/after-end rejected; timezone day rollover; missing/invalid timeline fails closed; cancellation ignores old deadline.</p></li><li><p>Optional contacts accepted; Vietnam local and international accepted; letters, double +, &gt;15 digits rejected; invalid email and non-HTTP(S) website rejected. Unknown contact keys preserved.</p></li><li><p>Backend bypass of UI receives field validation errors; UI shows matching errors and preserves input. vi/en keys parallel; semantic errors readable light/dark.</p></li><li><p>Do not run integration tests against Atlas or mutate shared test data.</p></li></ul><h2 id="verification-2026-10-14" tabindex="-1">Verification 2026-10-14 <a class="header-anchor" href="#verification-2026-10-14" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Verification 2026-10-14&quot;">​</a></h2><p>UI refinement: 9 Node unit tests pass (<code>node --experimental-strip-types --test --test-isolation=none tests/unit/request-deadline.test.mjs</code>, Node 24). Covers today/future start/expired/current whole day, Workspace day rollover, 23/25-hour DST days, invalid dates/timezone, differing browser timezone. TypeScript, targeted ESLint, build and locale parity pass. Playwright isolated mock confirms actual native min/max, underflow/overflow, inline error on invalid submit, valid last-minute save, expired/config failure save disabled, mobile dark date form. Real account end-to-end and browser-specific native calendar appearance remain manual checks. No database changes required for this UI refinement.</p><p>89 backend tests pass across ContentRequestAcceptanceMongoTest (14, owned ephemeral Mongo replica-set), ContentRequestCompletionTest (3), ContentRequestDeadlineTest (3), PartnerContactValidationTest (11), ContentRequestServiceTest (23), ContentRequestReviewServiceTest (13), CampaignDeploymentServiceImplTest (2), DirectoryPartnerServiceTest (12), ContentRequestCampaignGateTest (8). Frontend type-check and targeted ESLint pass. PostgreSQL fresh init and repeatable new migration run successfully in an isolated postgres:17-alpine container. No Atlas/shared data changed. Manual browser/theme checks remain pending.</p><h2 id="before-testing-locally" tabindex="-1">Before testing locally <a class="header-anchor" href="#before-testing-locally" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Before testing locally&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Back up PostgreSQL and stop Business Service writers. Apply only <code>docs/database/migrations/2026-10-14-content-request-completion.sql</code> to the intended existing PostgreSQL database (ON_ERROR_STOP=1). Do not rerun init. Restart Business Service with the migration present, then refresh UI. No new Mongo migration is required; the previously required Request V2/Acceptance migrations must already be applied.</p><p>Mark a test Campaign completed as Manager. New Request/create/update/receive fail immediately; the durable worker changes PENDING to CANCELLED on its next 5-second poll under healthy storage. History shows the Manager actor and CAMPAIGN_COMPLETED reason; IN_PROGRESS remains. Mongo downtime retains the SQL job for retry; no cross-database atomicity is claimed. Old Campaigns completed before this release are not automatically backfilled. Check pending jobs using <code>SELECT * FROM content_request_completion_jobs ORDER BY created_at;</code>.</p><p>The Request date picker remains native; the UI refinement adds min/max using Workspace day boundaries converted to browser-local input values. Server validation remains authoritative. 401/shared authentication is deliberately unchanged.</p>',9)])])}const h=a(r,[["render",o]]);export{m as __pageData,h as default};
